{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>In the seventh month.</b> For the reckoning begins from Nisan, for in it we went out from Egypt, and also because the barley aviv is first, then first fruits of the wheat harvest, then \"when you gather in your produce\" — and these appointed times depend upon being in the aforementioned days." "And since he said to blow the trumpets on every new month, behold <b>a remembrance of teru'ah</b> — and also \"a day of teru'ah\" — is a command to blow the shofar, and likewise on the Day of Atonements. And I, behold, will hint to you secrets, and set your mind, perhaps you will understand them. The translators said that the day of Rosh HaShanah is the Day of Judgment, and the reason for the teru'ah is a remembrance of the kingdoms of HaShem. And since the foundation is that all new moons — the first of Nisan was the honored new moon, for in it the Tabernacle was erected — and in the future Ezekiel said: \"In the first, on the first of the month,\" and likewise you shall do on the seven for the square, and behold the fifteen correspond, and the seventh day is also square, and the second Passover — the great and the small interchange. Therefore the day of Rosh HaShanah is greater than all of them, even though it is a day of judgment it is forbidden to fast on it, and Ezra proves it. And the Day of Atonements, the small one in connection. And behold, Sukkot is like the festival of Passover, only that there is an eighth and there is no seventh. From this the secret will be clear to you, and the secret of the Sabbath."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {1 "The syntax of the argument is extremely compressed throughout; several clauses are elliptical and possibly textually corrupt (e.g. 'and the second Passover — the great and the small interchange' lacks a verb; 'the small one in connection' is obscure). Rendered hyper-literally without smoothing. 'The translators' likely refers to the ancient Aramaic Targumim. The phrase 'the square' (המרובע) may carry a technical/kabbalistic sense left untranslated."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:12:01.700100721Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}